  "id": "2026/01/04/week-0-gym",
  "href": "/plan/2026/01/04/week-0-gym",
  "title": "Week 0: My Yearly Workout Wrap-up! 🎆💪",
  "date": "2026-01-03T22:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Week 0: My Yearly Workout Wrap-up! 🎆💪\n\nHappy New Year, everyone! ✨ This was actually my first time catching the fireworks in Tallinn! 🇪🇪 Last year I was stuck in the suburbs pet-sitting 🐶, so this was a nice change of pace.\n\nI’ll be honest—I didn’t do much \"tech digging\" this week. Most of my energy went into practicing German 🇩🇪 and grinding through work. But, I realized I still have one big topic to chat about: My fitness journey. 🏋️‍♂️\n\nSwitching things up from CrossFit 🔄\n\nFor the last five years, I’ve been a loyal follower of the CrossFit WOD. But lately? Not so much. Keeping up with a complex WOD in a crowded gym is a nightmare when people are hogging all the gear 🙄. Plus, the workouts started feeling a bit too easy.\n\nI decided it was time for a custom plan. My goal? Get a massive chest and wider shoulders. 🦍\n\nChest: Swapped the barbell for dumbbell bench presses (way better mind-muscle connection for me! 📈).\n\nShoulders: Spamming lateral raises for that width.\n\nCore: Yoga ball sit-ups and kettlebell rows to keep the midsection tight. ✨\n\nThe \"Thick Thigh\" Problem 👖\n\nI used to be obsessed with heavy squats and deadlifts, but I ran into a weird problem: My legs got too thick. 🍗 Seriously, I can barely find trousers that fit anymore! To lean them out, I’ve been doing trunk-carry running. Sadly, that means I’m putting thrusters, cleans, and jerks on the back burner for now. 🥲\n\nGetting back to my \"Roots\" 🍆😂\n\nI recently hopped on the hip abductor machine and it hit me... I remembered why I started gymming in the first place. It wasn't just to look good—it was to get my morning wood back! 🪵\n\nAround age 27–28, I noticed things weren't as \"upbeat\" as they used to be. I discovered that heavy leg movements are like a natural cheat code for blood flow and libido. 🚀 So, to get back to those original goals, I’m swapping the running for trunk-carry step-ups. Keeping the gains, but focusing on the functionality I care about. 😉\n\nThe Supplement Stack 💊\n\nCreatine: I used to think this was useless—just water weight, right? 💧 Well, a friend gave me his leftover tub, and I’m a convert. Not for the \"pump,\" but for the brain gains! 🧠 My memory and focus have been so much sharper.\n\nTongkat Ali: This was my go-to for the libido boost, but it’s a pain to find in Europe. 🇪🇺\n\nAshwagandha: Since I can't find Tongkat, I bought some Ashwagandha to try out. I haven't started it yet, but I'm curious to see if it lives up to the hype! 🌿",
